The PHY init values mainline ships for sm8550's gen3x2 QMP PCIe PHY differ from
what this board's own firmware uses.  The vendor kernel has no separate PHY
device at all: drivers/pci/controller/pci-msm.c replays the DT's
qcom,phy-sequence (82 offset/value/delay groups, final-runtime.dts:4645) into
the same 0x1c06000 window, and the ready bit it polls is the same
(qcom,phy-status-offset = 0x214, qcom,phy-status-bit = 6, i.e. the QMP
offset-0x14 status register's PHYSTATUS bit - the exact register mainline's
qmp_pcie_power_on polls after SERDES_START|PCS_START).

Mapping those 82 groups onto mainline's table layout (qmp_pcie_offsets_v5:
serdes 0x0 / pcs 0x200 / pcs_misc 0x600 / tx 0xe00 / rx 0x1000) leaves 71
groups byte-identical and 21 values different - all in the PLL programming
(SSC periods/step sizes, BG_TIMER, LOCK_CMP[12]_MODE[01] lock comparator
thresholds, DEC_START_MODE[01], DIV_FRAC_START[123]_MODE[01]) plus one TX and
one RX register.  With mainline's numbers the PLL never reports lock here, so
QPHY_PCS_STATUS keeps its PHYSTATUS bit set and every probe fails after
PHY_INIT_COMPLETE_TIMEOUT (10 ms):

  qcom-qmp-pcie-phy 1c06000.phy: phy initialization timed-out
  qcom-pcie 1c00000.pcie: probe with driver qcom-pcie failed with error -110

This applies the vendor's values.  For reference, the community port
(linux-sm8450-liuqin f88eb7add) makes a 26-line edit for the same purpose; it
matches the vendor in MODE1 but writes 0xff/0x06 for SSC_STEP_SIZE[12]_MODE0
(vendor 0xde/0x07) and 0xab/0xea/0x02 for DIV_FRAC_START[123]_MODE0 (vendor
0x55/0x55/0x03), and they report the controller probing but the modem never
appearing on the bus.

.lanes = 1 matches the single wired lane (the DT's num-lanes = <1>); the vendor
node has no num-lanes at all and reads LNKCAP from hardware.  With .lanes = 2
the driver also programs lane 2's TX/RX blocks.

Verified on the device (installed system running the kernel built from this
patch): the timeouts above are gone, the controller probes, and the chip comes up
- past what the community port reaches ("still no see"):

  pci 0000:01:00.0: BAR 0 [mem 0x60400000-0x605fffff 64bit]: assigned
  ath11k_pci 0000:01:00.0: wcn6855 hw2.1
  ath11k_pci 0000:01:00.0: chip_id 0x12 chip_family 0xb board_id 0xff soc_id 0x400c1211
  ath11k_pci 0000:01:00.0: fw_version 0x1106196e ... WLAN.HSP.1.1-03125-QCAHSPSWPL_V1_V2_SILICONZ_LITE-3.6510.37
  ath11k_pci 0000:01:00.0 wlp1s0: renamed from wlan0

and liuqin-wlan-mac.service (it waits for 17cb:1103) goes active.

